  "qualification": "Seven shared patch groups, 698 all-feature and 690 minimal-feature BRep/IO release tests pass after the final production edit. The later test alias correction is covered by final focused tests, strict Clippy and consumers. Affected strict Clippy/rustdoc, fuzz-target compilation and formatting pass. Source-path native consumers execute 107 groups plus eight original axial exchange workflows; actual zero-import WASM executes all 245 groups. All 354 prior native archives re-encode byte-identically; 115 STEP files import 125 bodies and replay; eight text controls are inventory-only. Fresh paired exports preserve exact values and structure: 177 byte-identical pairs and 105 explicit coefficient-encoding migrations across 2,952 scalar fields. Every export recipe repeats deterministically; 26 new patch archives also replay stably. The original nonorthogonal planar archive failure is reproduced on eaa0 and compared exactly to the corrected output.",
  "costs": "Three alternating pairs cover 92 preserved semantic rows; seven new groups have three absolute trials. All 57 processes pass their assertions. Observed time ratios range 0.852615\u20133.458309; 7 exceed the 10% review marker and 28 increase allocation calls or requested bytes. Selected-profile exports grow from 7,200,347 to 15,409,257 bytes. All adverse observations are retained. Shared-host instrumented samples, changed expression encodings and process RSS establish neither a byte-preserving optimization nor a general speedup or internal bound.",
  "limits": "Finite open-shell planar/extrusion patch support, not general embedding, selected revolution/axial parameters, curved arrangements, solid Boolean closure or complete CAD. First-export encodings intentionally change within schema 10; no compatibility reader. Total work, retained heap, coefficient growth and cancellation bounds, runtime fuzz/ASan/lexicase, formal coverage, MSRV, installed distributions and production bindings remain open. All 28 work packages remain open/in-progress. Full pre-push qualification remains required; the eaa0 one-time exception was consumed and does not authorize publishing this increment.",
  "source_reconstruction": "Recreate the base revision, decompress qualified-source.patch.gz, apply the resulting patch, and verify candidate-source.json. Final documentation-only changes are recorded separately. Retained consumer projects/locks and original inputs are in the lossless raw bundle; remap recorded source roots for a different checkout.",
